{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787341652073272001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"catlike-oversolemn-flee","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"943700b003cb7cf12c13e83a8d1132b3ffa6a487745767fc0caa5d9b064d8deb","event_uuid":"144de8e3-f056-485d-bdac-2bb253032e62","position":{"commit_sha":"68ca553dad9bf9e706957c7c15906f7fb8b396e8","position":"1787336921704316001-144de8e3-f056-485d-bdac-2bb253032e62"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"5a0dd1aaf42d0726c28ad21ef0903899a40311d2efff1b15a646ddaee27fe400","event_uuid":"d12a7ae4-8bf2-463a-b6be-2ba9a614bd3d","position":{"commit_sha":"79039570bc8143012465965f21c0c55eca2b9f31","position":"1787336936261981001-d12a7ae4-8bf2-463a-b6be-2ba9a614bd3d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787336921704316001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d12a7ae4-8bf2-463a-b6be-2ba9a614bd3d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b9b4-f460-2d54-4872"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` fails deterministically in this local macOS environment: `git -C <tmp>/bare.git cat-file -t <sha>` exits 128 inside the test's temp bare repo. Verified to fail IDENTICALLY on the untouched main checkout at 6fb4d801c9 with no local changes, so it is environmental/pre-existing, not introduced by any current work. At least six prior closed tickets note the same failure as 'known-unrelated' (e.g. 4522-e600-9e2c-4823, 7851-e06b-9e85-4c9e, 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6) but none left an open tracker, so every session re-diagnoses it.\n\n## Approach\n\nRoot-cause per /rebar-debug: reproduce deterministically, inspect why the object is absent from the bare remote after the push under this git version/filesystem (candidate mechanisms: partial-clone/promisor behaviour, fsmonitor, or APFS temp-dir quirk), and fix the CLASS (test or production ref-lock push), not the one run. No retry/skip band-aid.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause identified with a cited mechanism (recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] The test passes on this environment, or the incompatibility is fixed at its source — verified by running the test 5x locally.\n- [ ] Full reconciler suite green afterwards.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"02e8-96bd-82c1-45ff","ticket_type":"bug","title":"state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote fails on pristine main in local macOS env (git cat-file 128)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["144de8e3-f056-485d-bdac-2bb253032e62","d12a7ae4-8bf2-463a-b6be-2ba9a614bd3d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787341652073272001,"uuid":"0f09c132-448a-4f8d-9cea-926dc46d960f"}